//! `markise-md` — the Markise Markdown core (layer L1, spec `docs/spec/01-markdown-dialect.md`).
//!
//! Design (see `docs/adr/0001-markdown-core.md`):
//! - The Markdown text is the single source of truth. [`Document`] owns the text and a block
//!   tree ([`Block`]) whose nodes carry byte spans into it. Unchanged text is therefore always
//!   re-emitted byte-identically (R1.2–R1.4, R3.8.3).
//! - Edits are text patches ([`Document::edit`]). Structural operations ([`ops`]) compute the
//!   patch from the block's recorded pattern (R1.3); fresh blocks are generated by [`write`]
//!   using [`WriteOptions`].
//! - Re-parsing after an edit is incremental: it restarts at the nearest top-level block that
//!   began with no open container and stops as soon as the new parse re-synchronises with the
//!   old one.
//! - Inline content is parsed lazily, per block ([`inline`]).

